From be9b942274b0e534b1f23072f84fc1847290a582 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:11:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: LLM quota pacing governor holds claims when
 the pool is ahead of pace

Card t_01a1d975f57bb7b8 (follow-up of the 11-13/14 capacity incident t_01a1d96f7aecd229).

Why: on 11-12/13 the fleet (hub + workers 1-8) burned deep-class work at ~2.7x the Claude pool's
sustainable weekly rate (2.7-3.5B weighted tokens/day vs ~1.25B). One account-week went in under
21 h, 6 of 7 accounts reached seven_day 100%, Codex was walled for a week, and 301 worker starts
were refused overnight while nothing finished. Admission was gated on slots and walls only:
nothing slowed spawning as an account's week ran down.

What: before any claim, `_dispatch_lane_task` asks `kanban_llm_pacing_dispatch.hold`:
- The card's route comes from the read-only `resolve_dispatch_tier`; a class selector is held
  only when every subscription provider it may allocate holds it. Mandatory pins, unknown routes
  and ungoverned providers always start.
- Each governed pool (anthropic, openai-codex) is read read-only via `/api/oauth/usage` at most
  every 5 min per Hermes home; samples and this host's running count on the provider persist in
  `<kanban home>/llm_pacing.json`.
- Pool math (`kanban_llm_pacing`): per window kind (five_hour and seven_day, account-wide buckets),
  factor = sum(sustainable rate of headroom accounts) / sum(measured burn). Sustainable reaches
  95% exactly at that window's reset; burn is the steeper of the oldest/newest slopes over the
  last hour (fallback: the window's average). Factor < 1 = paced. Projection, not used-vs-elapsed:
  account-primary at 14:29:52Z on 11-14 was 92% used with 94.3% of the week elapsed ("behind pace")
  but rising 0.8%/min.
- Reserve: an account past five_hour 80% / seven_day 85% is left to chats, cron and notices; when
  every readable account is past it the pool is held until the earliest reset that frees one.
- Paced: this host keeps floor(factor x its average concurrency over the hour) runs on the
  provider; review-lane, negative-priority and scheduled-wake cards get half of that. Open but
  under factor 2: ramp to ceil(factor x avg), at least 1. Held: 0.
- A held card stays ready and unclaimed: `respawn_guarded` + `clock_held` reason `llm_pacing`
  (the stuck warning names the deadline), plus one `llm_paced` event per change/hour.
- Fail open on any read/resolve fault. `kanban.llm_pacing.enabled: false` = old behaviour.
  Knobs: target_percent, reserve_five_hour_percent, reserve_seven_day_percent, providers,
  read_interval_seconds, rate_window_seconds, min_rate_span_seconds, deferrable_share.
- Only the dispatcher imports it: chats, cron and notice delivery never consult the governor.

kanban_db_dispatch.py stays at its line count (two comments folded to offset the 3-line hook).

Proof:
- RED: with the 3-line hook removed, test_pool_ahead_of_pace_defers_spawns,
  test_held_pool_names_the_reset_and_repeats_no_event and
  test_only_kanban_dispatch_consults_the_governor fail; GREEN: 20/20 in
  tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_llm_pacing.py.
- 45 dispatch/tier/walls/quota/review/stuck test files: 718 passed.
- scripts/check --base origin/main: 20 checks ok.
- Live read on hermes-worker-8 (16:20Z 11-14): anthropic paced (6 accounts seven_day 100%,
  account-primary 5h 78%, account-secondary 7d 12% burning ~0.9%/min); openai-codex held until
  2026-11-20T22:40Z.
